WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.840
Hello, I'm Mr. Red.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.360
A horse is a horse, of course, of course, and no one can talk to a horse, of course,

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.000
that is, of course, unless the horse is the famous Mr. Red.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.760
Go right to the source and ask the horse, he'll give you the answer that you endorse.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:30.520
He's always on a steady course, talk to Mr. Red.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:36.200
Carol, where are you?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.840
In the kitchen.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.920
You shouldn't be working with that sprained wrist.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.480
I want to get dinner ready for Wilbur.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.480
Well let me help.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.480
Oh, thanks, Kay.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.480
Hand me the chicken, will you?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.640
It's in the refrigerator.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.400
One chicken coming up.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.560
Oh, no, I...

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:01.240
Oh, poor doll, he doesn't have a thing to wear.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.040
Just put it in the pot and light the stove.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:08.040
Oh, no, the little fellow's gone through so much already.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.160
Sweetie, why don't you let me prepare dinner for all of us tonight?

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:17.000
You know, salad, steak, mushrooms, apple pie.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Thanks, Kay.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.040
But I know you hate to cook.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.880
You're so right.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.880
We'll eat out, I'll call Addison.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.640
Okay, really.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.960
Wilbur's on the phone.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.960
Thank you.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.480
I'll have your address, yes.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.080
And Velma, it'll just be for the one week, eh?

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.000
There won't be much housekeeping to speak of.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.200
Most of your work is gonna be done in the kitchen.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.200
Cooking.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.880
All right, I'll pick you right up.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.880
Thank you, goodbye.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.160
Well, Ed?

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.840
Gisoon, hi.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:02:00.320
Carol's gonna be surprised when she finds out I've hired a cook to help her.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.640
That's the trouble with us Americans, we spoil our women.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.760
Oh, come on, Carol's a great cook, you know that.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.400
It's just that she sprained her wrist.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.520
Sure, how did she sprain it?

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.800
The can opener slipped.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.200
Gisoon, hi, again.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:21.120
Velma Pinkney, she sounds very efficient.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.120
Thank you very much.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.120
You're welcome.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.720
You know, I think I'm allergic to your hay.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.400
What are you complaining about?

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:35.000
I have to eat this stuff.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:43.280
Wilbur, did you call that cook I recommended?

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.280
Just going now to pick her up.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.280
Good.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.080
I hope you didn't tell Kay about my surprise, because she is sure to tell Carol.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.080
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.320
I learned my lesson 20 years ago when I told Kay a secret.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.320
What secret?

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.320
That I was single.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.320
I should have known.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.240
Look, we want you and Kay to be our guests tonight for dinner.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.840
I mean, the way you talk about this Velma, she must be a wonderful cook.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.200
Oh, she is, great.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.280
But that's the story of my life.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.880
The only time I ever get a good home-cooked meal is when I go to somebody else's...

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:07.880
Go to somebody else's house.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:17.600
Married men.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:28.120
Boy, am I glad I'm a bachelor.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.120
This is it, Velma.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.120
I'll tell Mrs. Post you're here.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.120
You'll be surprised.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.120
Honey?

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.120
Carol?

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:42.240
Hi, dear.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.240
Surprise for you, honey.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.560
Say hello to Velma, our new cook.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.960
She's going to be with us for a week.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.640
Oh, thank you, darling.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.640
Hello, Velma.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:50.640
Hello, Mrs. Post.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.640
You happy?

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:57.600
Oh, darling, you're the most wonderful husband in the world.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.840
One thing about my wife, Velma, she always tells the truth.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.720
Oh, hang on to it, Mrs. Post.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.960
A good man is hard to find.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.360
Any man is hard to find.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.680
At my age, even a bad man is hard to find.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.640
Well, there'll be four for dinner tonight, Velma.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.200
I invited Roger and Kay over.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.160
Well, I know you'll be happy here.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.160
Be in my office, dear.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.160
Okay, dear.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.160
I'll show you to your room.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:26.280
Oh, what a nice man.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.080
Mrs. Post, have you got a butler working for you?

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.080
No.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.080
A chauffeur?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.080
No.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.560
Well, on my day off, it looks like solitaire again.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:41.440
Oh, by the way, do you have your milk delivered?

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:42.440
Yes.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:43.440
Is the milk man married?

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:44.440
He has kids.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:45.440
You don't have to rub it in.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.440
Color feast.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.440
Velma, this dinner is delicious.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.440
Oh, thank you.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.440
Marvelous.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.440
Oh, it's perfect.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:51.440
I'd never do anything like it.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.440
This wasn't a dinner.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.440
This was a banquet.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:05:01.640
Oh, this meal is so beautiful.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:02.640
I could wear it.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.200
That soup is a collector's item.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.800
Oh, honey, thanks again for Velma.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.960
She's the nicest present you've ever given me.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.280
She were a little smaller, I would have had her gift wrapped.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.560
Wilbur, can I open a charge account here?

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.680
Oh, no, darling.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.100
We mustn't take advantage.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:18.680
We should meet here over four or five times a week.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.320
Thank Alaska.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:25.760
Oh, beautiful, beautiful.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:31.720
Velma, your hand should be immortalized at Grauman's Chinese.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:35.440
Oh, Mr. Fose, thank you.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.560
The good ones are always married.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.960
Thank you.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.160
Thank you very much.

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:45.200
Oh, Velma's such a jewel.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.160
I wonder why the Johnsons let her go.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.280
She quit.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:52.120
I understand she was engaged to the butler Henry and they broke up.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.480
Oh, that's too bad.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:54.480
She's such a nice woman.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.320
I hope she finds somebody.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:59.480
If you wouldn't mind, my dear, I'd marry her myself.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:00.480
She'd cook for us.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.480
I'd let you.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.800
Sure going to hate to lose her at the end of the week.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.600
Well, if it'll make you feel any better, honey, I'll sprain the other wrist.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.600
Please?

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.080
Oh, boy, pizza.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:16.200
It's for your horse, Mr. Post, a carrot pizza.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.200
For your horse?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.040
Yeah, he loves Italian food.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:25.480
He's got sugar cubes, I have to feed him breadsticks.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:41.160
Oh, you like Velma's pizza, huh?

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.960
When I worked at the Johnsons, so did my boyfriend Henry.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.600
He ate like a horse, too.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.360
He should only choke.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.960
Do you know I fed that man like a king for four years?

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.120
And what happened?

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.800
I got the brush.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:59.640
Man, who needs him?

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:13.200
I do.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.200
Henry's loss is my gain.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:22.200
Man, this pizza is molto bene.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.200
Santa Lucia.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.200
Santa Lucia.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:39.000
This is your last homemade pizza, Ed.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.720
Carol's wrist is better and Velma's leaving tonight.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.200
Not so loud.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:48.080
I don't want my stomach to know it's back to hay again.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.080
You know, she sure fattened you up.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.080
Wow.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:54.960
Another week, you'll have to get a girdle for you.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.680
Don't let her go, Wilbur.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.800
My friends say I never look better.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.560
I'm going to try to talk her into staying last night, but she wants a job where she

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:03.560
can meet men.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:07.200
All right, throw a USO dance for her.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.840
I might just do that.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:10.840
Last piece.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:18.880
There's only one thing that would make her change her mind, if she met a man.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.240
And that's one thing you can't buy at the supermarket.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:24.440
How about the postman, Mr. Hodges?

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.440
Married.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.040
The plumber?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.040
Married.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:35.120
Do you think she'd wait for the newsboy to grow up?

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.440
I'm ready to leave, Mr. Post.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:38.400
Will you drive me to the bus station?

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:39.400
Sure.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:46.920
Now, Velma, if you weren't leaving, what would you be cooking for dinner tomorrow?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:51.640
I was going to start with little individual cheese souffles.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.080
Cheese souffles.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.360
Cheese souffles.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.560
Artichoke hearts with sour cream dressing.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.240
Sour cream dressing.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.680
Sour cream dressing.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:05.680
Then?

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:10.120
My main course would be a tornado of beef with Bearnaise sauce.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.120
Bearnaise sauce.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.120
Bearnaise sauce.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:16.960
And for dessert?

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:17.960
Cherries Jubilee.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:24.400
Cherries Jubilee.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.440
What are we having for dinner tomorrow?

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.920
I'm not sure.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:34.600
The label washed off the can.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:35.880
Goodbye, Mrs. Post.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.720
It was so nice working for you.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.560
Well, if you ever change your mind...

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:40.560
Excuse me.

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:41.560
Hello?

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.560
Yes, she's here.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.560
Velma, it's for you.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.560
A man.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:45.560
A man?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.560
Hello?

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.560
Yes, this is Velma.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.560
Who's this?

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:49.560
Walter.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.560
Walter who?

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.560
Just call me Walter.

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:52.560
Until we know each other better.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:53.560
Walter.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:54.560
Walter.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.560
Walter.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.560
Walter.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.560
Walter.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:58.560
Walter.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.560
Walter.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.560
Walter.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:01.560
Walter.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:02.560
Walter.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.560
Walter.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.560
Walter.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:05.560
That's even better.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:06.560
Who are you?

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.280
Just a secret admirer.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:14.040
What do you want?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:19.640
I've watched you from a distance and I adore you.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.600
I don't speak to strange men.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.600
Are you married?

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.920
I've never trotted down that middle aisle.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:30.120
He sounds like a Harvard man.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.280
What do you have in mind?

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.680
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:34.880
Will you be there?

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.680
Of course I'll be here tomorrow. I'll be here all week.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:38.800
I work for the Post.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:40.260
Yes?

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.400
Cherries.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:42.960
Chupuli.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:44.960
Cheese souffle.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:51.760
Hello, Ed.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.600
Hello, Wilbur.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:58.000
Isn't it wonderful about Velma finding a boyfriend and staying?

00:10:58.880 --> 00:10:59.200
Yeah.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:01.120
Just a minute.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:05.040
Uh, here's the menu I wrote out for my dinner tonight.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:05.920
Dinner?

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.400
Oat cocktail.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.200
Home fried carrots.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:17.440
Baked apple with alfalfa sauce.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:17.680
No.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.680
And lobster thermidor.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.800
Lobster thermidor?

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.040
That's in case you want to eat with me.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.480
Oh, you're very thoughtful.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:32.640
Just give Velma the menu and leave her a good tip.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.480
Well, later, Ed. I got work to do.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:35.040
All right.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:37.520
Lobster thermid...

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:39.760
Lobster thermidor.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.120
Wilbur!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.040
Velma is leaving!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.480
What, again?

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.320
But what happened? She said she'd stay.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.280
Remember that phone call she got from that fellow Walter last night?

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:56.160
Well, he didn't call back, so she's packing.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:57.600
Maybe I better have a talk with her.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:59.920
I don't think it'll do any good. She's made up her mind.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.040
Well, I guess Walter has to turn on the old charm again.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.080
Velma?

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.000
Yes, Mr. Post?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.960
Velma, can't we sit down and talk this over?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:21.840
Mr. Post, the only reason I stayed, I was expecting a call from that fellow, Walter.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.160
But there are other men.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.320
Yeah, and I'm going looking for them.

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:30.160
Maybe I could break our TV set and ask for a bachelor repairman.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.760
With my luck, he'd be 90 years old.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:36.160
No, I'm ready to go now, Mr. Post.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:40.160
Oh, goodbye, Mrs. Post. I enjoyed working for you.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.360
Well, good luck, Velma.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.520
Oh, wait just a minute, please.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:48.660
Hello?

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.280
Yes, she's here.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.680
Velma, it's for you.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:57.360
A man.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:12:59.140
Hello?

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.520
It's me, my love, Will.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.200
What happened? I was waiting for your call.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:08.560
I, uh, I just lost my nerve.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.440
Oh, you're shy.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.040
Oh, we're perfect for each other.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.440
I'm shy, too.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:23.680
Cherished jubilee?

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:27.200
Well, goodbye, my love. I'll call you tomorrow.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.800
Tomorrow? If you don't meet me tonight, I won't be here.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:36.080
Uh, then it's tonight. I'll meet you outside the patio after dinner.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:38.100
Good.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.720
Oh, I, I hope you're as handsome as you sound.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:45.920
I am, but it all depends on your point of view.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.920
Au revoir, chérie.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:58.960
Almost eight o'clock.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.680
I hope that Walter shows up.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.760
The girls have been up there working on Velma for an hour now.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:09.520
I certainly hope they've prettied her up a little.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:13.760
Velma deserves happiness. You know, she has so much to offer a man.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:16.240
Friendship, warmth, loyalty.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.160
Stroganoff, lasagna, shish kebab.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.320
If she leaves, I'll kill myself.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.920
Well, she'll be right down.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:25.440
How does she look?

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:26.960
Anxious.

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.280
I can't even get a hold of you if we're going to make that movie.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.680
Yeah. Roger, would you mind looking in on Ed?

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.440
Make sure that barn window's closed.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:34.400
Oh, sure, sure.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:48.400
Here she comes.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.880
Velma, you look beautiful.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:51.760
Oh, Mr. Potter.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.240
Beautiful? She's positively enchanting.

00:14:58.400 --> 00:14:59.520
Won't you be late for the movie?

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:01.280
Oh, yes, yes. Come on, honey, let's go.

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:02.240
Have a nice time, Velma.

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:03.040
Have a good time.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:03.600
Good night, Val.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:04.880
Thank you. Good night.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.400
Velma, have fun.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:27.360
Have a good evening, Velma.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.080
Is that you, Walter?

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.440
It's me. You look beautiful, Velma.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:46.800
Why don't you come over here where I can see you?

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.520
I told you, I'm shy.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:52.720
Don't be like that.

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:57.760
We're all alone.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.520
Don't come any closer, Velma.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:08.480
Oh, why, Walter?

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:18.000
You don't have to be that shy.

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:20.800
Hello, Velma.

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:22.900
You...

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.240
You ought to be ashamed of yourself.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:27.600
For doing this?

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:29.680
Does your wife know?

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.600
Of course, I just told her.

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:33.520
Well, I'm not that broad-minded.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:39.200
What's the matter with that woman?

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:43.040
What's she talking about, broad...

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:46.960
What's the matter with me talking to a horse?

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:59.680
He had to show up.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.920
Now I'm back to hay again.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:11.700
Velma!

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:17.780
Is Romeo here?

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.000
Who?

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.860
Your husband, our boyfriend.

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.060
What are you talking about?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.140
When he complimented me and kissed my hand,

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:29.780
I thought he was only after my cooking.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:30.660
Addison?

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.580
I'll be your witness in court.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:33.540
Oh, now, just a minute.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.580
There must be a mistake.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:38.260
Ask your husband what happened in the backyard.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:39.300
What did happen?

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:40.580
Let Walter tell you.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.540
Walter?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.980
That's your husband.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:47.300
Now, Velma, I'm sure you must be mistaken.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:48.580
I don't want to hurt your feelings,

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:51.620
but I just can't imagine my husband leaving me for...

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:52.340
For me?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.340
Mrs. Addison, I may not be as pretty as you,

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.700
but when it comes to cooking,

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.300
you can't hold a pot to me.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.940
Oh, now, darling, really?

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.540
Just because I'm not a good cook

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.940
and my husband happens to enjoy your cheese soufflés,

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.700
your baked Alaska and your wonderful gravies,

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.660
and what did happen in the backyard?

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:11.700
Let him tell you.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.700
Dear, it's getting late.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.420
Should we turn in?

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:24.600
Hey!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.100
Are you crazy?

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:36.900
Here, have some juice, dear.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:37.700
Thank you.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:41.220
I can't understand why Velma hasn't been down to fix breakfast.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.260
She must have overslept.

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:45.220
Her boyfriend probably kept her out late.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.180
Oh, not again.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:52.500
Mr. Post, I'm leaving.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.340
But, Velma, you promised to stay.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:54.840
Velma.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:57.540
What happened?

00:18:57.540 --> 00:18:59.220
Didn't Walter show up last night?

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.380
Yes, Mr. Addison did.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:02.600
Addison?

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:06.360
You might as well know your neighbor is a chaser.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.160
Oh, Velma, really?

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:11.960
Underneath that mustache, you'll find a blue beard.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.800
Velma, I think you're imagining all this.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.600
Why, Mr. Addison is very devoted to his wife.

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:20.920
Why, he wouldn't think of looking at another woman.

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:23.320
Mrs. Addison believed me last night.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.280
Kay would never believe a story like that.

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:28.040
I wouldn't say that.

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:30.600
Velma?

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.600
Please, haven't you done enough?

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.680
Roger, what's going on here?

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.320
She told Kay the most fantastic story.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.440
How, how, how, how I...

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:42.200
Why don't you take your crummy pizzas and go?

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.640
Oh, now, Roger, just a minute.

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.040
Her pizzas are not crummy.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.760
I'm going home to mother.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.680
Oh, now, Kay, dear.

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:55.320
I hope that you and Velma and her soufflés, the three of you, will be very happy.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:56.920
Kay, please.

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.440
Now, just a minute, Kay.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:01.160
I'm sure there's a perfectly logical explanation for this.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:02.920
Tell her, Roger.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:06.680
Of course, I'm Walter.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:08.200
I've been Walter for 20 years.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:10.120
I am also Bluebeard.

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.400
I'm, I'm, I'm Jack the Ripper.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:11.900
I'm, I'm...

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:12.400
Hello?

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.640
Yes, she's here.

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:19.720
Velma, it's for you.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.000
A man.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:25.180
Hello?

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.740
It's me, Walter.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.740
Walter?

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:33.980
What happened last night?

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:34.700
See?

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:35.900
It couldn't have been Roger.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.940
I never doubted you for a minute, doll.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:39.900
I'm sorry.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:41.100
You're sorry?

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:45.900
I don't know who she was talking to last night.

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:47.820
There was just me and the horse.

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:49.820
What did you say, Walter?

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:53.420
I'm sorry I had to leave so suddenly last night, Velma.

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:57.900
Yes, well, I'll try to understand.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.500
I don't think I'm...

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:00.300
No, for you.

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:00.940
Oh, Walter.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.860
Well, I'm kind of a drifter.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:07.180
You need a man with a steady job.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:10.700
A fine girl like you needs a real man.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:11.260
Oh, Walter.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:13.420
My trouble is, I'm not a real man.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:14.140
I'm a real man.

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:14.700
I'm a real man.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:15.260
I'm a real man.

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:15.820
I'm a real man.

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:16.380
I'm a real man.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:16.860
I'm a real man.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:17.900
My trouble is...

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:18.940
Yes?

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:20.220
Uh-oh.

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:26.160
Hello?

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:27.200
What?

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:28.080
Hello?

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:31.020
Oh, he hung up.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:33.340
Oh, now I'm all mixed up.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.220
Velma, now sit down.

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:37.260
Don't you worry.

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:38.780
Now just calm down.

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:48.620
Excuse me a minute, dear.

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:49.260
How do you do?

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:51.180
I'm Henry Gibson.

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:52.700
I work for the Johnsons.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.300
Is Miss Velma in?

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:54.800
Yes.

00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:57.020
Velma, come in, please.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:02.700
Well, this is the worst trick you have ever pulled.

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:03.740
But Wilbur, I...

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:05.260
Do you know you broke that woman's heart?

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:05.900
But Wilbur...

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:07.180
And look what you did to the Addisons.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:07.980
But Wilbur...

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:09.500
All because of your big appetite.

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:10.140
But Wilbur...

00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:12.140
All right, go ahead.

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:13.100
It's your turn.

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:15.820
If only Perry Mason were here to defend me.

00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:18.300
You ought to be ashamed of yourself.

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:22.800
Wilbur!

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:24.160
Wilbur!

00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:26.780
Guess what?

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.300
Velma is engaged.

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:29.580
To Roger?

00:22:30.940 --> 00:22:31.740
Stop.

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:33.900
Henry, the Johnsons butler that she was going with,

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:36.140
just showed up and proposed.

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:37.500
Well, that's wonderful.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:38.940
Come on, she wants you to meet him.

00:22:38.940 --> 00:22:40.540
Yeah, well, I'll be there in a minute, honey.

00:22:46.540 --> 00:22:47.900
This is lucky for you.

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.180
But Wilbur...

00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:51.980
I was going to send you to bed tonight without any supper.

00:22:51.980 --> 00:22:55.820
But Wilbur, who do you think called the Johnsons

00:22:55.820 --> 00:22:58.540
and got Henry Gibson over here to propose?

00:22:59.260 --> 00:22:59.760
You.

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:02.220
How did you do it?

00:23:02.220 --> 00:23:05.340
I told him somebody was running off with his girl

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:08.620
and if he liked her cooking, he'd better hurry right over.

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:11.020
But Ed, why didn't you tell me?

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:13.340
Because you bawled me out.

00:23:13.340 --> 00:23:13.900
But Ed...

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:16.380
Besides, who can get a word in with you around?

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:17.900
But Ed...

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.900
You're always jumping to conclusions.

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:20.960
But Ed...

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:24.860
But Ed, but Ed, is that all you can say?

00:23:26.620 --> 00:23:27.120
But Ed...

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:29.120
Ed...

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:37.200
May I propose a toast to Kay's first home-cooked meal?

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:39.200
Thank you very much.

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:40.240
Congratulations, Kay.

00:23:40.240 --> 00:23:57.520
I hope it's all right.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.880
Well, so much for experimentation.

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:07.520
Well, it's not really bad.

00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:09.040
Once you get it down.

00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:14.320
My dear, no offense, but would you mind if we celebrated

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:16.960
your first home-cooked dinner at Pierre's restaurant?

00:24:18.480 --> 00:24:21.360
Why, doll, I've already made the reservations.

00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:35.360
They're off to a fancy restaurant and I'm back to barn-cooked meals.

00:24:51.360 --> 00:24:55.680
Go right to the source and ask the horse, he'll give you the answer that you endorse.

00:24:55.680 --> 00:24:59.360
He's always on a steady course, talk to Mr. Ed.

00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:03.440
He will yakety-yak the streak and waste your time a day.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:07.680
But Mr. Ed will never speak unless he has something to say.

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:12.560
A horse is a horse, of course, of course, and this one will talk to his voice's horse.

00:25:12.560 --> 00:25:14.720
You never heard of a talking horse?

00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:17.920
Well, listen to this.

00:25:17.920 --> 00:25:25.280
I am Mr. Ed.

00:25:25.280 --> 00:25:45.760
This has been a Filmways television presentation.
